  "_": "Hand-authored site data (like rules.json), NOT generated. Colours are a finish choice, not a file: nothing here may reference a release artefact. Every entry is an OPAQUE base colour — see _palette.",
  "_palette": "ONE palette of opaque base colours, shared by band, tray, plate (printed path), keycaps, switches, toppers and the LED lighting — there is no reason a colour that exists for the band cannot exist for the plate. The set is the filament shelf: neutrals, metals, the full saturated spectrum with light/dark steps, pastels, earths, neons. TRANSLUCENCY IS NOT A COLOUR: it is an independent per-part checkbox (state.<part>.translucent) that renders the chosen colour through the one treatment below, so a frosted-clear look is translucency + a pale colour and a smoked look is translucency + a dark one. That is why there are no trans_* or crystal entries here.",
  "_palette_order": "The order IS the layout: the picker drops a GRID of swatches 8 wide (round 4: 'why not drop down a grid of swatches? Then you can have more colors'), so this list reads as 7 rows of 8 — neutrals, darks+metals, earth+warm pastels, reds->yellows, greens, blues, purples+neons. Reordering rows here reorders the grid.",
