  "_translucent": "The ONE translucent treatment, used by every part whose translucency checkbox is ticked. Round 4, verbatim: \"transparent should be translucent -- and it should be more opaque than this. A frosted look is more like what it is\", then \"Not opaque but a little more so.\" So this is FROSTED PRINTED PLASTIC, not clear acrylic: the transmission comes down a step and the roughness goes up a lot, which is what scatters the transmitted image instead of refracting it sharply. The high roughness is also what turns the LED ribbon behind the band into a broad soft wash rather than a readable hard line. Transmitted light is still tinted by the part's own colour, so this single material reads as frosted glass under a pale colour and as smoked resin under a dark one — which is why the palette needs no translucent entries of its own. Viewer material only; it reaches no file and no order.",
  "translucent": {
    "transmission": 0.78,
    "thickness": 3.2,
    "ior": 1.5,
    "roughness": 0.55,
    "clearcoat": 0.35,
    "clearcoat_roughness": 0.28
  },
